      "text": "To find the area of a circle with a given diameter, we start by recalling the formula for the area of a circle:\n\n\\[\nA = \\pi r^2\n\\]\n\nwhere \\( r \\) is the radius of the circle. The radius is half of the diameter. Given that the diameter is 4 meters, we can find the radius as follows:\n\n\\[\nr = \\frac{4}{2} = 2 \\text{ meters}\n\\]\n\nNow, substitute the radius into the area formula:\n\n\\[\nA = \\pi (2)^2\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\( 2^2 \\):\n\n\\[\n2^2 = 4\n\\]\n\nSo, the area \\( A \\) becomes:\n\n\\[\nA = \\pi \\times 4 = 4\\pi\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the circle is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{4\\pi}\n\\]",
